# Julie Sufi - version 11 developer environment configuration
# Rename to .env if required by your deployment setup.
# This is NOT a complete export of the existing production secrets.
# Keep private. Do not commit this file to Git or serve it from the website.

# Owner-provided admin password:
ADMIN_PASSCODE="27081996"

# REQUIRED: generate a fresh signing secret for the NEW hosting environment.
# Run: openssl rand -base64 48
# Paste the output between the quotes below. Blank = admin login unavailable.
# A new signing secret invalidates previous admin sessions.
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=""

# Required when configuring Instagram.
# To decrypt migrated Instagram settings, obtain the EXISTING encryption key
# through an authorised secure transfer. It is not readable via this export.
# Alternatively, for a fresh Instagram setup, run: openssl rand -base64 32
# Paste the output below, then configure/reconnect Instagram on the new host.
# A new key CANNOT decrypt Instagram settings encrypted with the old key.
INSTAGRAM_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# Cloudflare deployment notes:
# Configure these values as Worker secrets in the destination account.
# For Wrangler local development, use the appropriate .dev.vars / environment
# configuration and ensure values are exposed in cloudflare:workers env.
# Merely placing this file in the repository is not a production deployment.
#
# DB and BUCKET are D1/R2 resource bindings, NOT string environment variables.
# Configure those bindings separately in the destination Worker configuration.
# No database, uploaded media, Meta app credentials or access tokens are included.
# Meta app credentials are entered in the admin Instagram setup.
# Update the Instagram origin/callback in lib/instagram.ts for the new domain.
